  "query_preview": "..Mostly dry and stable conditions will persist\nthrough at least Saturday with seasonal temperatures. The one\nexception to this being across portions of southern/southeastern\nUtah where some elevated moisture will keep slight chances (<25%\nchance) for diurnal thunderstorms through Friday.\n\nSouthwesterly flow starts to increase this weekend ahead of an\nincoming trough. This trough will be our next chance for\nwidespread precipitation. Hurricane Polo in the eastern Pacific\nwill make a track to the north as it heads towards the Baja \nCalifornia peninsula. This will help to supply the incoming trough\nwith tropical moisture, if the trough takes a certain trajectory.\nCurrently, 31% of ensemble members (an increase from the previous\nforecast package of just 23%) bring the trough a bit further south\nacross the Great Basin late Sunday into Monday. This track would\nbe far enough south to really pull in that tropical moisture into\nUtah resulting in widespread precipitation and potentially\nflooding concerns. The other 69% of ensemble members keeps the\ntrough a bit further north resulting in a drier solution and most\nof the precipitation going into eastern Utah and Colorado/New\nMexico.",
